{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1473923530,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxNzcxMDU1NzM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/833","origin":"github"},"title":"How to deal with `uninstall` requests that are not undoable","message":"Currently there is `--remove-history` a dedicated flag that needs to be given, if a repository is completely wiped out. And there is `--nocheck`, that currently makes datalad ignore git annex complaining about an insufficient number of copies of files to be dropped.\n\nHowever, there is another condition: Removing subdatasets that progressed past the point that they have been recorded in the parent with. Demo based on code based on #832 \n\n```\ncrcns (git)-[master] % git submodule |grep ac-1\n c1cd8599c3c87fea8128fcb9f8bc1b0e299f3e6b ac-1 (heads/master)\ncrcns (git)-[master] % datalad uninstall -r --remove-handles --remove-history ac-1\n2016-09-15 08:59:12,404 [ERROR  ] Cannot delete module at /home/mih/hacking/datalad/DONTLOOK/datasets.datalad.org/crcns/ac-1 as there are new commits [base.py:remove:838] (InvalidGitRepositoryError) (main.py:259)\n```\n\nI can force that already, by not going through the parent\n\n```\ncrcns (git)-[master] % datalad uninstall -d ac-1 --remove-handles --remove-history\n1 item was uninstalled:\nDataset: /home/mih/hacking/datalad/DONTLOOK/datasets.datalad.org/crcns/ac-1\ncrcns (git)-[master] % git st\nOn branch master\nYour branch is ahead of 'origin/master' by 3 commits.\n  (use \"git push\" to publish your local commits)\nChanges not staged for commit:\n  (use \"git add/rm \u003cfile\u003e...\" to update what will be committed)\n  (use \"git checkout -- \u003cfile\u003e...\" to discard changes in working directory)\n\n    deleted:    ac-1\n```\n\nand a subsequent `save -a` of the parent will simply deinit the submodule (at which point we admit that those changes are (intentionally) lost.\n\n```\ncrcns (git)-[master] % datalad -l debug save -a\n2016-09-15 09:09:17,330 [DEBUG  ] Resolved dataset for saving: \u003cDataset path=/home/mih/hacking/datalad/DONTLOOK/datasets.datalad.org/crcns\u003e (dataset.py:504)\n2016-09-15 09:09:18,784 [DEBUG  ] deinit deleted subdataset ac-1 in \u003cDataset path=/home/mih/hacking/datalad/DONTLOOK/datasets.datalad.org/crcns\u003e (save.py:74)\n....\n```\n\nIt kinda makes sense, but it doesn't feel quite natural. Any suggestions?","files":null}]}